Module larum "The Quiet in the Sky" {
  // ── The Morning After ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // At first light after the Testing day the horns sound, or they do not. Then the book closes on what the forty days
  // made, and on the Field; and the Field goes on.
  Query accounting() means outcomeDecided(field_country) and morningAfter() and hour(clock) >= 7.
  Chapter ch_after_field "The Morning After" when morningAfter() and hour(clock) >= 6 and inYsgard(party) "First light on the Field. Everyone on it, the living and the dead, is listening for the same thing.".
  Chapter ch_after_larum "The Morning After" when morningAfter() and hour(clock) >= 6 and not inYsgard(party) "First light in Larum. Everyone in the street is standing with their heads on one side, looking up at the Pass.".
  Rule horns_sound within field_country when morningAfter() and hour(clock) >= 7 and outcomeDaily(field_country) and not spoke(horns_told)
    says "At the third horn they come down off both heights, Morrow from the east and Even from the west, as they have every morning for nine hundred years, and meet on the ford, and the noise goes up off the Field like a flock of birds. It goes over Halt. Halt does not slow it. By noon the shield-walls are down and the banner lanes are trodden into the snow, and the Oven's mantlet is on its side, and the Daily goes on over the place where the town was as if it had never been there." { Assert spoke(horns_told). }
  Rule horns_half_even within field_country when morningAfter() and hour(clock) >= 7 and outcomeHalf(field_country) and halfByEven(field_country) and not spoke(horns_told)
    says "At the third horn Evenhall comes down the stone stair to the ford, and turns on itself, and begins: Even against Even, the Daily with one side. On the eastern height Morrowhall's doors stay shut. And in Halt, a mile from the ford, the dead of Morrow stand in their lanes listening to it, and go on with what they were doing, and the sound of it goes over them every day after that, like weather." { Assert spoke(horns_told). }
  Rule horns_half_morrow within field_country when morningAfter() and hour(clock) >= 7 and outcomeHalf(field_country) and halfByMorrow(field_country) and not spoke(horns_told)
    says "At the third horn the doors of Morrowhall open, and Morrow comes down off the eastern height to the ford, because Hild Varley knows now that there is nothing to be afraid of, and does not know what else Morrow is for; and finds no Even there, and turns on itself, and begins. Even stays at its benches and in Halt, and listens to it, every day after, like weather." { Assert spoke(horns_told). }
  Rule horns_silent within field_country when morningAfter() and hour(clock) >= 7 and (outcomeHalt(field_country) or outcomeQuiet(field_country) or outcomeFear(field_country)) and not spoke(horns_told)
    says "The third horn does not sound. Nor the first. The sun stands low in the white where it always stands, and the Field lies under it with nobody on it but a few Runners with a sledge, and in Halt the smoke goes up from the Oven, and somebody is laughing in the banner lanes." { Assert spoke(horns_told). }
  Entity horns_told: fact "the morning after".
  Rule larum_hears_loud within larum when morningAfter() and hour(clock) >= 7 and skyLoud() and not spoke(larum_told)
    says "Down off the Pass, out of the standing cloud, faint as bells three valleys off, it comes: iron on iron, thousands of it. Larum stops in the street. A woman puts her hand to her mouth. Then somebody laughs, and somebody else, and the shepherd with the walnut face says, 'There. There, now,' as if to a ewe; and by noon nobody is listening to it, and that night Bet Garside sleeps until ten." { Assert spoke(larum_told). }
  Rule larum_hears_quiet within larum when morningAfter() and hour(clock) >= 7 and not skyLoud() and outcomeDecided(field_country) and not spoke(larum_told)
    says "Nothing comes down off the Pass. Larum stands in the street with its head on one side and listens to nothing, as it has for forty-five days. Then Bet Garside comes out of the Hark with her two dented pans, and looks at them, and hangs them up on a nail by the door." { Assert spoke(larum_told). }
  Entity larum_told: fact "Larum's morning".

  // ── What the forty days made ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Rule fate_bread when accounting() and breadRisen(grimbold) and not spoke(fate_bread_told) says "Grimbold Ure bakes every morning at three, as his father did, and the Runners carry flour up from Larum a sack at a time, and Nance Pellett's Mother lives in a crock on a shelf above an oven built out of a broken bell, two hundred and some years old, in heaven. On the Field they still say nothing rises but the dead; and then they say, and Grimbold's bread." { Assert spoke(fate_bread_told). }
  Rule fate_bread_daily when accounting() and breadRisen(grimbold) and outcomeDaily(field_country) and not spoke(fate_bread_daily_told) says "When the Daily trampled Halt the Oven went over with it. Grimbold carried the crock up to Morrowhall inside his shirt, against his chest, where it is cold, and it died there before the Hour. He goes down to the Field every morning by the third horn with the rest of Morrow. He does not go mad any more. He is not much good." { Assert spoke(fate_bread_daily_told). }
  Rule fate_wedding when accounting() and wedded(mab) and not spoke(fate_wedding_told) says "Mab Treloar and Ansel Haverlock keep a tent in the banner lanes, of a black bird on gold that somebody picked off the Field. He bows to her every morning, the little bow. She has never once spat." { Assert spoke(fate_wedding_told). }
  Rule fate_wedding_daily when accounting() and wedded(mab) and outcomeDaily(field_country) and not spoke(fate_wedding_daily_told) says "On the first morning of the Daily, Mab Treloar and Ansel Haverlock did not go down to the ford. They went north, up the stair on the Old Ice, to sit with the Sitters and learn to play stones; and they are there still, and the halls have forgotten them, which they say is very restful." { Assert spoke(fate_wedding_daily_told). }
  Rule fate_paired_only when accounting() and paired(mab) and not wedded(mab) and not spoke(fate_wedding_told) says "Mab Treloar and Ansel Haverlock meet at the ford at noon, every day, with nothing in their hands, and talk. Nobody has married them. Nobody knows how." { Assert spoke(fate_wedding_told). }
  Rule fate_song when accounting() and songMade(wystan) and not spoke(fate_song_told) says "Wystan Hollins's song about the sheep is sung in Halt by people who have forgotten who made it, which is how he says he likes it. He has made two more since, both bad. He is working on a third." { Assert spoke(fate_song_told). }
  Rule fate_elegy when accounting() and elegyMade(wystan) and not spoke(fate_song_told) says "Wystan Hollins's elegy for Halvard Eld is the best thing he ever made. Larum has it in print within the month, at a penny a sheet, and it sells in three countries; and wherever there is a war in Imbar, men sing it going in." { Assert spoke(fate_song_told). }
  Rule fate_runners when accounting() and runnersSeated(cuddy) and not spoke(fate_runners_told) says "There is a bench in Morrowhall, the low one by the door, where the Runners sit with horn cups while the hall eats. Cuddy Wardle sits at the end and swings her legs. Morrow hates it. Hild Varley says, good." { Assert spoke(fate_runners_told). }
  Rule fate_strike when accounting() and runnersStrike(cuddy) and not runnersSeated(cuddy) and not spoke(fate_runners_told) says "The Runners did not go out with the sledges that night, nor the next, and nobody on the heights knew what to do about it, because nobody had ever imagined they could say no. Cuddy Wardle has been to both halls since, in a clean smock, by the front door." { Assert spoke(fate_runners_told). }
  Rule fate_sitters when accounting() and sittersDown(aulus) and not spoke(fate_sitters_told) says "The Sitters play stones on the floor of the Truce every evening, surrounded by the dead of both halls arguing about the rules. Aulus has found Cassian, in Morrow, after seven hundred years. They are not speaking. They play every night." { Assert spoke(fate_sitters_told). }
  Rule fate_plough when accounting() and ploughMade(gorm) and haltStands() and not spoke(fate_plough_told) says "On the southern Field, where the battle-lines never quite reached, there is a strip of ground scraped clean of iron and turned over with a plough of four swords, and something has been sown in it from a sack carried up from Larum. Nobody knows yet whether anything will come up in Ysgard. Gorm Hallett goes out every morning to look." { Assert spoke(fate_plough_told). }
  Rule fate_ned_halt when accounting() and haltStands() and knows(party, ned_dead) and not spoke(fate_ned_told) says "In Cleeve's ledger, after nine hundred years of EAST and WEST, there is a third column now, ruled in fresh ink: HALT, for those who come in with no hour. The first name in it is Ned Whitlock's." { Assert spoke(fate_ned_told). }
  Rule fate_ned_daily when accounting() and outcomeDaily(field_country) and knows(party, ned_dead) and not spoke(fate_ned_told) says "Ned Whitlock, who came in at noon, went to the Runners in the end, because there was nowhere else; Cuddy Wardle took him on the sledges. Every night after the Hour he drags the broken off the ford, a boy with a blackthorn stick tucked in his belt." { Assert spoke(fate_ned_told). }
  Entity fate_bread_told: fact "the bread". Entity fate_bread_daily_told: fact "the bread under the Daily". Entity fate_wedding_told: fact "the marriage".
  Entity fate_wedding_daily_told: fact "the marriage under the Daily". Entity fate_song_told: fact "the song". Entity fate_runners_told: fact "the Runners".
  Entity fate_sitters_told: fact "the Sitters". Entity fate_plough_told: fact "the plough". Entity fate_ned_told: fact "Ned".
  Rule fate_jory when accounting() and joryMet(jory) and not spoke(fate_jory_told) says "Jory Whitlock goes up through the White every seventh day, in his good coat, and sits with his son a few hours, and comes down before the cold. He does not say much about it in Larum. He has stopped laying the second cup." { Assert spoke(fate_jory_told). }
  Rule fate_jory_untold when accounting() and knows(party, ned_dead) and not joryTold(jory) and not spoke(fate_jory_told) says "In Larum Jory Whitlock still lays two cups, and the mule is in the byre, and nobody has told him." { Assert spoke(fate_jory_told). }
  Entity fate_jory_told: fact "Jory".
  Rule fate_edith_home_shaken when accounting() and edithHome(edith) and edithShaken(edith) and not spoke(fate_edith_told) says "Edith Marl went down the valley road on foot. A chapman says a woman with fuller's hands keeps a stall at Wendham market, selling cloth; and that once a year, in the summer of the bad wool, she shuts it and walks to where Wendmere was, and stands there, and does not say whom for." { Assert spoke(fate_edith_told). }
  Rule fate_edith_home when accounting() and edithHome(edith) and not spoke(fate_edith_told) says "Edith Marl went down the valley road on foot and was not heard of again in Larum, except that a chapman said a woman with fuller's hands had taken a stall at Wendham market, selling cloth, and would not have the ballad sung within earshot." { Assert spoke(fate_edith_told). }
  Rule fate_edith_killed when accounting() and edithDead(edith) and toroldKilledEdith(torold) and not spoke(fate_edith_told) says "Edith Marl came in out of the snow an hour after Torold Hame's sword, and Cleeve sent her west, into Evenhall. Torold was waiting at the foot of the stone stair. He has not lifted a sword since. He brings her a cup of mead every evening, at the end of the lowest bench, and she drinks it, and neither of them has said a word to the other, and they sit there." { Assert spoke(fate_edith_told). }
  Rule fate_edith_dead when accounting() and edithDead(edith) and not spoke(fate_edith_told) says "Edith Marl came in out of the snow in the afternoon, and Cleeve sent her west, into Evenhall, where Halvard Eld's name runs up the Tally from the floor to the roof. She sits at the end of a bench and does not fight and does not speak, and Torold Hame brings her a cup of mead every evening, and she drinks it, and neither of them says anything at all." { Assert spoke(fate_edith_told). }
  Rule fate_edith_unknown when accounting() and at(edith, edith_nook) and not knows(party, edith_named) and visitedBefore(warren) and not spoke(fate_edith_told) says "In the Scrapes, behind a banner, there is a woman in three Runners' smocks whose breath goes up white in the lamplight. She has learned the sledges. Nobody on the Field has asked her name." { Assert spoke(fate_edith_told). }
  Rule fate_edith_hidden when accounting() and at(edith, edith_nook) and knows(party, edith_named) and not spoke(fate_edith_told) says "Edith Marl is still in the Scrapes, in three Runners' smocks, shivering. She has learned the sledges. The Runners say she is better at them than most of the dead." { Assert spoke(fate_edith_told). }
  Entity fate_edith_told: fact "Edith".
  Rule fate_torold_ice when accounting() and buriedIce(torold) and not spoke(fate_torold_told) says "Torold Hame goes up to the Old Ice every evening at the Hour, and stands with his hand flat on the clear ice over his friend's face while the blue comes over, and then comes down." { Assert spoke(fate_torold_told). }
  Rule fate_torold_larum when accounting() and buriedLarum(torold) and not spoke(fate_torold_told) says "Torold Hame stands at the Coming-in every evening at the Hour, at the edge of the snow, and listens; and down in Larum the parson rings the Mending Bell, three times, and now he knows for whom." { Assert spoke(fate_torold_told). }
  Rule fate_torold_none when accounting() and state(halvard, lying) and knows(party, halvard_fell) and not spoke(fate_torold_told) says "Halvard Eld lies in the ring of spears in the middle of the Field under his frost. Torold Hame stands over him. At the Hour, every evening, he watches the face for it, and it does not come." { Assert spoke(fate_torold_told). }
  Entity fate_torold_told: fact "Torold".

  // ── The endings ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Ending ending_halt "Halt" when accounting() and outcomeHalt(field_country) "They know now. Nothing came back to the Field but what came up the Pass, and they could go down to the ford by the third horn tomorrow and every day after and get up at the Hour every evening until the stars go out. They do not. They stay at their benches and their ovens and their swapping-blankets, Morrow and Even and Runner and noon, because forty days have given them something they would rather do. It is not safe, and it is not finished. It is only chosen. In Larum, below, it is quiet, and the Mending Bell rings at dusk, and everybody knows why.".
  Ending ending_quiet_known "The Long Quiet" over ending_quiet when accounting() and outcomeQuiet(field_country) and knows(party, living_kills) "Nobody on the Field knows what killed Halvard Eld. They believe death has come back to Ysgard, for all of them, and so the horns stay silent, and Halt grows, a tent at a time. It is a peace. It stands on not knowing. A breather knows what it stands on, and has not said, and goes down through the White to Larum, where it is quiet, carrying it.".
  Ending ending_quiet "The Long Quiet" when accounting() and outcomeQuiet(field_country) "Nobody on the Field knows what killed Halvard Eld, and nor, quite, do you. They believe death has come back to Ysgard, for all of them, and so the horns stay silent, and Halt grows, a tent at a time. It is a gentle peace, made of fear and spoons, and nobody knows how long it will last, and nobody asks.".
  Ending ending_fear "The Kept Fear" when accounting() and outcomeFear(field_country) "They saw a man of Even lie on the ford at the Hour and not get up, and they know now that death has come back to Ysgard, and the horns will never sound again. Halt will grow into a city. They will make bread and songs and marriages in it, and teach their children, if the dead ever have children, that the Field is death. It is a good peace, and it will last. You are the only person in either world who knows what it is made of. When you go down through the White your breath goes up in front of you, and you watch it, and do not look back.".
  Ending ending_half "Half a Field" when accounting() and outcomeHalf(field_country) "The Field is a war with one side now. Every morning one hall comes down and fights itself on the ford, and every evening gets up, and the other hall sits in Halt a mile away and bakes and swaps and listens to it, the way you listen to rain. Nobody can say whether this is better. Larum, below, hears the sky again, a little fainter than before, and says it is not the same noise.".
  Ending ending_daily_unseen "The Daily" over ending_daily when accounting() and outcomeDaily(field_country) and not visitedBefore(halt_cross) "Somewhere over the Pass, on the fourth morning, the men of Even went down to the ford and fought each other, and at the Hour every one of them got up, and so nothing had come back; and the next morning the horns sounded on both heights. Whatever the quiet was, it is over. In Larum the shepherds do not look up any more. You stood once at the head of the Pass, in a light like the inside of a knife, and looked down at a huddle of coloured tents in the middle of a white plain, and did not go down to see what they were.".
  Ending ending_daily "The Daily" when accounting() and outcomeDaily(field_country) "Every man of Even got up at the Hour, and so nothing had come back, and in the morning the horns sounded at the third hour on both heights, and the Field was what it had always been. Halt is snow and rags. The Oven is on its side. In Larum the noise is back, faint as bells three valleys off, and Bet Garside sleeps, and the shepherds do not look up any more, and nobody but you remembers that for forty-five days there was a town on the Field where people learned to make spoons.".
}
